  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize exposing Aces. If an Ace is trapped under two high cards (like a King and Queen), you will likely need to rely on the shuffles to free it.\n\nThe King Trap: Avoid moving a card onto a King unless absolutely necessary. Since Kings are the highest cards, they can never be moved onto another card, meaning any card underneath a King in a fan is potentially permanently blocked.\n\nStaged Progression: Don't move every possible card to the foundations immediately. Sometimes it is better to keep a card on the tableau to serve as a 'landing spot' for a lower card of the same suit.",
    Player: "Prioritize exposing Aces. If an Ace is trapped under two high cards (like a King and Queen), you will likely need to rely on the shuffles to free it.\n\nThe King Trap: Avoid moving a card onto a King unless absolutely necessary. Since Kings are the highest cards, they can never be moved onto another card, meaning any card underneath a King in a fan is potentially permanently blocked.\n\nStaged Progression: Don't move every possible card to the foundations immediately. Sometimes it is better to keep a card on the tableau to serve as a 'landing spot' for a lower card of the same suit.",
